  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building on progress in tackling the illegal trade of endangered wildlife in Vietnam</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to, (1) Reduce demand for wildlife and wildlife products with a focus on high priority species including tigers, rhinos (horn), elephants (ivory), marine turtles, and pangolins; (2) Mobilize public action in efforts to stop wildlife crime and reduce consumption of wildlife; (3) Reduce consumer crime in major urban centers of Vietnam by expanding crime reduction campaigns which include reporting crimes to district level Peoples Committees and providing these committees a period of 60-90 days to address violations leading to a report card for each district, followed up by progress check on violators, etc.; (4) Disrupt and disable criminal networks engaged in the smuggling and trade of wildlife, by updating profiles on major criminal networks; (5) Strengthen wildlife protection policy and legislation; and (6) Strengthen ENVs role as representatives and the voice of civil society in Vietnam, by participating in CITES Cop17 focusing on rhino horn, tiger, and pangolin trade issues, and exchanging information with South African law enforcement.</narrative>
  </description>
